Speaker 1: Let's talk about today's mass shooting.&nbsp;
I guess it's actually yesterday's, but what a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:15.760
country that when we say the mass shooting, I have&nbsp;
to speculate. Not the one from last Tuesday and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:22.320
not the one from the previous weekend. I'm talking&nbsp;
about the one from yesterday. Another horrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:29.840
event. Four people have been killed in a mass&nbsp;
shooting at a Tulsa, Oklahoma. It's sometimes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.400
being discussed, this described as a hospital,&nbsp;
maybe more accurately, a medical building.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:44.160
The gunman is also dead. CBS News has a report&nbsp;
that contains much of the information. We now know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.280
four people were killed in a shooting last night,&nbsp;
Wednesday evening in a medical building on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:55.440
